WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.590
A phone lies flat on a
table, showing a photo.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.950
Pick it up and turn it sideways.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.930
The photo swings round to fill the screen.

4
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.410
Now take it into a dark cupboard
and turn it on its side.

5
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.390
The picture still turns.

6
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.050
So how does it know which way up it is?

7
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.670
Is it finding north, like a compass?

8
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.610
In this mission, you'll see how a
sensor measures a physical property,

9
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.990
like temperature, and
sends the reading as data.

10
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.990
You'll find your phone contains
several different sensors,

11
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.430
and each one measures one thing.

12
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.370
Then you'll choose the right sensor for
jobs from greenhouses to swimming pools.

13
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: explain how your
phone knows which way up it is.
